ed for human detection, pose estimation, and person re-identification tasks simultaneously.', 'A multi-task network utilized by FastPose, integrating pose estimation, keypoint detection, and person Re-ID tasks.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2]}, 'Pose Estimation': {'description': ['The task of determining the position of key body joints in an image or video.', 'A computer vision task that involves determining the position and orientation of objects or people in an image.', 'The task of estimating the pose of a person in an image or video.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2]}, 'Person Re-identification (Re-ID)': {'description': ['The task of identifying and tracking individuals across different camera views or time instances.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 2]}, 'SIFP (Scale-normalized Image and Feature Pyramids)': {'description': ['A paradigm proposed to address the scale variation problem in pose estimation, improving both performance and speed.', 'A paradigm designed to handle scale variations in unified pose approaches, improving performance.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 2]}, 'Feature Pyramid Networks (FPN)': {'description': ['A network architecture used to extract features at multiple scales.', 'A method that proposes a pyramidal representation and fuses adjacent scale feature maps to combine features with semantic and detail information.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1]}, 'SIFP (Scale-normalized image pyramid and feature pyramid)': {'description': ['A paradigm exploited to alleviate the scale variation problem of MTN, using both image and feature pyramids.', 'A paradigm designed to handle scale variations in unified pose approaches, improving performance.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 2]}, 'Person search datasets': {'description': ['Datasets composed of images within multi-person and corresponding ID annotations, used for training head networks.', 'Da